     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day), and the maximum for a single dose is about 1,000 mg. This order is double the daily maximum, and it carries a real risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity even with normal kidney function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** That could be 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** For example, 500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose.\n\nTell me the intended dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
