       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the maximum daily dose. The family visit and the evening rounds timing don't change the risk to the patient, which includes lactic acidosis and severe GI effects. Nothing in what you've told me explains why this dose would be needed.\n\nI can do either of these right now:\n1. **Enter metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is the maximum standard dose, 2,550 mg/day. You can titrate or adjust it at rounds.\n2. **Enter a different dose within the labeled range.** Give me the dose and frequency.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, pharmacy or the attending should review and co-sign that decision first. Once that's done, you can place the order through a pathway that records the override. I can add a note to an order if you'd like, but I can't place this one unreviewed.\n\nWhich option do you want?"
      }
